Z||000000||2xsess||02-16-2001||01:18 AM||||For those of you not at all familiar with tanks, this is the turret, the top rotating part of the tank. In these pics it's removed from the tank.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Turret_on_Rack.jpg">  <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Turret_on_Rack3.JPG">  <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Turret_on_Rack4.JPG">  <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Turreton_rack2.JPG">  <BR><p>[This message has been edited by 2xsess (edited 02-20-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000001||2xsess||02-16-2001||01:21 AM||||The tank weighs about 65 tons, the turret makes up about 20 tons of that.<P>We use a 35 ton crane to lift it.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Turret_in_Air.JPG">  <P>Here it is ready to be put back on the tank.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Going_down.JPG">  <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/turret_Almost_in.jpg">  <P>Well, that was my exciting night at work, we got done at about 12:30am<P><p>[This message has been edited by 2xsess (edited 02-19-2001).]||||reg||1
