Z||000008||2xsess||02-16-2001||10:25 AM||||You guys crack me up.<P>Sorry all you duke fans but it's a 1500hp turbine engine. Top speed is about 60 mph.<P>track mod...LMAO.<P>Ross, t-top models are very rare, it does have duel sunroofs though  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> does that count?<BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>AOL IM : Only2xsess<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2xsess.gif">      <BR> <A HREF="http://kresgeus.homestead.com/FieroPage.html" TARGET=_blank>Visit My Website</A>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Raydar||02-16-2001||10:43 AM||||How many lateral G's on the skidpad? Stopping distance from 60-0?<P>One of those would come in handy for Atlanta traffic.<P>Great pics. My dad was a tank mechanic in France, in WWII. Usta work on Shermans. <BR>I feel old, now.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 02-16-2001).]||||reg||12
Z||000010||Hank is Here||02-16-2001||12:03 PM||||Those turrets are just held on by gravity right?  <P>Oh yeah do you have any dyno sheets to back up the 1500 hp claim, seems to me there isn't enough stickers to have that much power.||||reg||1
Z||000011||2xsess||02-16-2001||12:22 PM||||Steve, I work with a guy that was a tanker on the Shermans so don't feel old yet.<P>Hmmm...an M1A1 in Atlanta traffic,  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> sounds like fun to me.<P>No, they're not held on by gravity, there are about 50 bolts that hold it down around the diameter.<P>The sitckers are on the inside, putting them on the outside would totally ruin the camo effect. Do posters of naked women add more hp than the usual HKS and etc. stickers?<P>As far as dyno sheets, if you can find a dyno that can handle that thing let me know, I'd like to see it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>AOL IM : Only2xsess<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2xsess.gif">      <BR> <A HREF="http://kresgeus.homestead.com/FieroPage.html" TARGET=_blank>Visit My Website</A>||||reg||1
Z||000012||william_thorniii||02-16-2001||04:02 PM||||2x,<P>I actually was looking at a dyno page the other day that claimed they worked for "tread-driven vehicles".  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||14
Z||000013||Hank is Here||02-16-2001||04:35 PM||||For what it is worth, It is legal in Texas to drive tracked vehicles on the road  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Also you can register a tank, half-track there and need no license plate because you can paint the plate number on it like unit marknigs and it's legal.  Regristration for these is under $200 if I remember correct, also it in not necessary to carry insurance on classic military vehicles there.  Don't ask me why I know this  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000014||TheFiero64||02-16-2001||04:42 PM||||Cool, If you can drive tracked vehicles on the road in Texas then I am moving and buying a M-577. I drove those when I was in the MA National Guard. I will have to find a picture of one so you all know what the hell I am talking about. It had no mounted weapons, but it was a hell of a lot of fun to drive off road.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||10
Z||000015||2xsess||02-16-2001||05:41 PM||||Josh, I think the M-113s are much more fun to drive, they're not as high. But yes they're all fun to drive. <P>A dyno for track vehicles, hmmm...interesting.<P>I don't think I want to move to TX anymore, it's wierd enough seeing Bradleys and Tanks rolling around here but out on the streets would really freak me out.<P>Oh and as far as economy, it gets 8 gals to the mile. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> yes re-read it lol.<P>Personally I'd rather have the duke ||||reg||1
