Z||000026||RNGCRSH||02-20-2001||12:21 AM||||When I was in the military working on F-18's any picture with an open panel or exposed sub-assembly would have been classified as secret, meaning taking a picture and making it available to the general public would have been considered treason and was punishable by life in prison. You would be surprised at what our enemies can get from one photo.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>Most of what is on websites listing specs on military vehicles is correct, but many times The government leakes misinformation in addition to correct data. About 35% of the stats for the f-18 I see on websites, tv shows, and magazine articles are grossly wrong. Especialy when in regards to power, armor, speed, armorment, and electronics. <p>[This message has been edited by RNGCRSH (edited 02-20-2001).]||||reg||1
